.TH geectl-build-abort-build 1  "geectl-build-abort-build 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-abort\-build \- Abort the running build of a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the abort
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build abort\-build\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Abort the running build of a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the abort
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to abort the build for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
